<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  🔴 THIS FILE EXISTS FOR ONE KEY, AND THE OBVIOUS ALTERNATIVE FAILS
	     SILENTLY.

	  `INFOPLIST_KEY_UIBackgroundModes = "audio voip"` in the build settings
	  looks right, is accepted by xcodebuild, and shows up in
	  `-showBuildSettings` — and then does NOT appear in the generated
	  Info.plist at all. Xcode's generator only honours an allowlist of
	  `INFOPLIST_KEY_*` names and `UIBackgroundModes` is not on it. There is
	  no warning anywhere.

	  The consequence is exactly the failure that is hardest to diagnose:
	  PushKit registers, the app looks healthy, and VoIP pushes are simply
	  never delivered — so an incoming call never rings and nothing logs a
	  reason.

	  `GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE` stays YES: with `INFOPLIST_FILE` also set,
	  Xcode MERGES its generated keys into this file, so every existing
	  `INFOPLIST_KEY_*` setting still applies and only this key lives here.

	  ⚠️ It lives at the REPO ROOT, not in `VirtualSIM/`. That folder is a
	  `PBXFileSystemSynchronizedRootGroup`, so anything inside it is also
	  copied in as a bundle resource — which collides with its use as
	  `INFOPLIST_FILE` and fails the build with "Multiple commands produce
	  .../VirtualSIM.app/Info.plist". Keep it out of the synchronized folder.

	  Verify after any project-file change, because this cannot be caught by
	  a build succeeding:
	      plutil -p "$APP/Info.plist" | grep -A3 UIBackgroundModes
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
		<string>voip</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
